    <statement><p>Convert from polar to rectangular coordinates:</p>
<p><m>\mathbf{(a)}\quad(5,\pi)\quad\Rightarrow_{(x,y)}\quad</m>(<fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/>,<fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0002"/>)</p>
<p><m>\mathbf{(b)}\quad(7,\frac{\pi}{6})\quad\Rightarrow_{(x,y)}\quad</m>(<fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0003"/>,<fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0004"/>)</p>
<p><m>\mathbf{(c)}\quad(5,\frac{\pi}{3})\quad\Rightarrow_{(x,y)}\quad</m>(<fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0005"/>,<fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0006"/>)</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6.06218</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3.5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2.5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4.33013</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\mathbf{(a)}</m> Since <m>r=5</m> and <m>\theta =\pi</m>, we have:
<me>x=r\cos\theta=5\cos \pi=5\cdot -1=-5</me>
<me>y=r\sin\theta=5\sin \pi=5\cdot 0=0</me>
<me>\Downarrow</me>
<me>(x,y)=(-5,0)</me>



<m>\mathbf{(b)}</m> For <m>(7,\frac{\pi}{6})</m> we have <m>r=7</m> and <m>\theta=\frac{\pi}{6}</m>. Hence,
<me>x=r\cos\theta=7\cos \frac{\pi}{6}=7\cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}=6.06218</me>
<me>y=r\sin\theta=7\sin \frac{\pi}{6}=7\cdot \frac12=3.5</me>
<me>\Downarrow</me>
<me>(x,y)=(6.06218,3.5)</me>



<m>\mathbf{(c)}</m> Since <m>r=5</m> and <m>\theta =\frac{\pi}{3}</m>, we have:
<me>x=r\cos\theta=5\cos \frac{\pi}{3}=5\cdot \frac12=2.5</me>
<me>y=r\sin\theta=5\sin \frac{\pi}{3}=5\cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}=4.33013</me>
<me>\Downarrow</me>
<me>(x,y)=(2.5,4.33013)</me>


</solution>
